---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Technical Collaboration Path';
const description = 'The technical route for collaborating with DeathEmpire: workspaces, branches, pull requests and security rules.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en" enPath="/DeathEmpire/contributing/" esPath="/DeathEmpire/es/contributing/">
  <article>
    <header>
      <p class="section-eyebrow">FOR TECHNICAL READERS</p>
      <h1>Technical Collaboration Path</h1>
      <p>This is the technical route. If you are looking for creative, testing or support collaboration, start at <a href="/DeathEmpire/collaborate/">Collaborate</a>.</p>
    </header>
    <section>
      <h2>Workspaces</h2>
      <p>The project is organized in coordinated workspaces: coordination, public site, private automation, game services, regional servers and entry proxy. Public workspaces are listed under <a href="/DeathEmpire/repositories/">Open Development</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Working Branches</h2>
      <p>Use dedicated branches per change, opened from the corresponding main branch. Small, reviewable branches are preferred over large rewrites.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Pull Requests</h2>
      <p>Pull requests are the main way to land changes. They are peer-reviewed and must pass automated validations before merging. Features still marked as designed should be treated as experimental until fully validated.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Never Publish Secrets</h2>
      <p>Never publish secrets, tokens, IPs or other operational information in public documentation.</p>
    </section>
    <footer>
      <p><a href="/DeathEmpire/collaborate/">Back to Collaborate</a> · <a href="/DeathEmpire/project/">The Project</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
